WEBVTT

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:04.190
In this place so unreal

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:07.820
I wait for dawn to come

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:12.950
Farther and farther, like the sky I saw that day

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.210
What a joke this hope is

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:22.750
I acted as if I had forgotten

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.260
Farther and farther, like the dream I saw that day

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:34.140
I just want to know the meaning of it

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.310
Within this scattered time

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:41.100
Along with the breath of ours

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:45.070
And of this pain that never goes away

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.610
Even though the roaring of the sea muffles the voices

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:52.490
Darkness engulfs everything ahead

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:56.540
The light that passes through our fragile hearts

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.960
Won't go away

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:03.750
We only relied on our compass

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:07.920
We believed you

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:14.760
While we stand here

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.890
We're searching for the unseen future

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:29.860
Zipang

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.690
It's on top!

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.070
You're not bad.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:40.530
Mori! It's our turn next...

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:42.580
Mori...?!

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:49.210
Order of Attack

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:59.050
Ensign Mori! Answer me!

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:02.560
Tell me your date of birth! The year, the month, and the day!

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:07.140
I remember you're born in 1982, September 3rd, a Virgo, right?

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:11.400
Which year do you think this is? It's 1942, you know!

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:15.610
If you're born in 1982 and died in 1942...

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:17.490
...the numbers don't add up!

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:19.910
Don't die! Stay alive!

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.830
Felt like a hit... but not hard enough.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.080
I'll finish them off!

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:44.260
Sea Fowl, Fortune Inspector! Image is lost!

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:46.060
What happened?! Umidori!

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:48.520
Situation report now!

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:51.020
Lieutenant Satake! What's happening?!

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.190
This is the...

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:56.150
Sea Fowl.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:58.360
The cockpit... has been hit.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.410
- What?!
- The Ensign is...

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:02.280
What's happened to Ensign Mori?!

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:06.040
Bullet wound... Bleeding...

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:10.750
Retreat at full speed! Shake off the Japanese fighter planes!

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.290
Can you do that?

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:14.750
Target is two planes. We're completely trapped.

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.670
There's no way.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:21.220
Executive Officer, please issue the order for attack!

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:24.180
Ensign Mori needs immediate medical attention!

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:26.640
Please let me counter their attack!

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:30.520
The opponents are Japanese, too!

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:35.270
Is there a need for us... to be killing our own people?!

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:36.900
Back at the cafeteria earlier,

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:39.280
you said that this ship was our country, right?

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:41.820
If we're attacked, it's only natural to fight back!

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:43.780
Please issue the order now!

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.620
The floats...

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.500
If the floats are destroyed, its balance will be disrupted,

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.540
and attacking will not be possible.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:58.670
Moreover, the float also holds the fuel tank for that fighter plane.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:02.340
Even if it could still fly, it can only fly half as far as before,

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:05.090
so it'll never reach this ship here.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:09.850
I think that plane is capable of aiming for the floats.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:11.890
Aren't you an Imperial Soldier yourself?!

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:14.310
How do we trust someone who's willing to betray his own country?!

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:17.900
We are all Japanese. I want to save the life of the other passenger.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:20.860
Commander Kadomatsu, I'm sure you want that too, right?

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:25.870
Sea Fowl, permission to fire!

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:29.120
However, you're only to aim for the opponent's float!

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:31.750
Satake, I know you're capable of this.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:34.500
Executive Officer, is that an attack order?

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.750
That's right, an order for attack.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:40.090
However, it's my first time firing in a real battle.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:42.840
There's a possibility I might hit something other than the floats.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.840
I won't allow that!

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:47.010
I trust your skills.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:51.640
Roger. Connecting Vulcan to Eye Link System!

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:56.850
Connection established!

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.570
Target in range. Alright!

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:07.110
Ready to fire anytime.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:10.870
Propeller pitch variable. Blade angle tilt 60 degrees!

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:14.370
80 degrees!

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:15.830
Here I come!

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:19.540
It... vanished?!

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:22.800
It's below? Trying to escape with a sudden descent?

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:25.260
It's not there? Where is it?!

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:31.260
This is for Mori!

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:37.060
Target is locked on.

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.600
Fire!

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:46.900
Oh, no! I can't maintain my balance!

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:34.740
Come on, let's go back now, Ensign Mori!

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:40.000
You know, the SDF has never lost a man in battle.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.540
And from now on too.

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:45.130
Fortune Inspector, Sea Fowl.

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:47.590
Both targets have been successfully taken down.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:49.800
Both pilots unharmed.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.720
End of report.

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:54.720
Medical team, stand by!

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:07.490
This is the result of consecutive revolutions,

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:09.570
sudden ascents, and sudden descents.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:11.110
The rivets have come out.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:13.320
The frame might be out of shape, too.

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:16.410
Put on the gauge for an ultrasound stress scan.

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:17.200
Yes!

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:18.660
I must hand it to...

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:22.080
...Lieutenant Satake for coming this far without a G suit.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:27.800
Chief, is this from a 7.7 mm machine gun?

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:30.300
Yes. I think Ensign Mori...

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:34.350
never expected to engage in a Zero-Type battle in his dreams.

00:07:57.790 --> 00:08:00.120
Please let me do the introductions.

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:04.750
Lieutenant Commander Kusaka will assist us as advisor to this ship.

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:06.920
I am Kusaka. Pleased to meet you all.

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:15.970
We have abandoned the thought of docking at the Yokosuka Base.

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:18.430
This ship was originally scheduled for...

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:21.930
...refuel and re-supply at Pearl Harbor.

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:24.100
Regarding the issue of supplies,

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:26.560
I'd like you all to hear Lieutenant Kusaka's suggestion.

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:31.940
As this ship requires a special type of fuel,

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:34.110
rather than mainland Japan,

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:36.740
I feel it is more advisable for us to obtain this fuel...

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:40.200
...from one of the Japanese colonies in the south.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:44.750
Oil production is the richest on Palembang, an island of Sumatra,

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:48.340
with Singapore's naval port situated nearby.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.670
The military base housed in Singapore,

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:54.880
is the Second Fleet under the command of Admiral Kondo.

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:57.930
Because of participation at Midway earlier on,

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:00.510
there are only a few light cruisers...

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:03.390
...and destroyers anchored at port.

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:08.230
The conditions for replenishing this ship is most favorable.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:12.070
For a start, we'll stop and hide this ship in the Anambas Archipelago,

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:15.530
80 nautical miles northeast of Singapore.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:17.700
I'll fly to Sumatra's Port of Mersing...

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:19.870
...with a carrier-based aircraft from this ship,

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:23.040
and proceed south to enter Singapore by land.

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:25.870
Then I will make contact with the military base stationed there.

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:28.210
After I acquire a civilian vessel,

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:30.960
I will secure the needed food and fuel supplies,

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:34.220
and proceed to meet up with this ship in Anambas.

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:36.970
That's the brief run through of this operation.

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:39.510
The documents required for the acquisition...

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:41.510
...can be prepared on this ship.

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:44.520
Of course, I will provide guidance on that.

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.940
By the way, you're proceeding ashore alone?

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:50.230
If that worries you, 2 or 3 men can go with me.

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:51.520
But then...

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:54.150
That means we'll be forging documents...

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:56.110
...to cheat the army of its supplies, right?

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:58.070
Are you sure about this?

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.540
If we have to resort to violence,

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:09.710
prepare for a skirmish worse than the Ogasawara incident.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:13.380
- Any further questions?
- Lieutenant.

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:16.220
You're supposed to be killed in action at Midway... no.

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:18.380
Or rather, missing in action.

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:21.100
Nevertheless, you're still a soldier of the Imperial Army.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:23.260
This is an infringement of the military law.

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:26.390
You may face court martial. Are you prepared for that?

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:30.440
Imperial Navy Lieutenant Commander Kusaka...

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:33.730
...has lost his life out at sea.

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:37.860
The work that I do here is not for the Imperial Navy.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:41.410
As with all of you, it is for the country Japan,

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:43.580
and for the future to come.

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:13.480
You have done well.

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:21.780
If you have to, blame me instead.

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:24.490
I was the one who refused to give the attack order till the very end.

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:28.330
I refused to accept the fact that we were caught in the midst of war.

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:30.460
I didn't want to lose the meaning of being an SDF officer.

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:34.170
Please wake him up and explain that to him yourself!

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:37.500
That he was... not a soldier!

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:48.600
I understand. This is all my fault.

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:50.520
I started thinking about my grandfather in Ogasawara,

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.440
and was caught off guard.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:56.940
It's my fault for wanting to fly low in spite of the risk of being seen.

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:59.740
He tried his best to stop me!

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:01.650
I'm sorry, Executive Officer!

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:13.460
The captain came by?

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:17.880
No, Lieutenant Kusaka came by when no one was around.

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:20.670
Kusaka? Did he say anything?

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:22.220
No, nothing.

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:24.800
He kept silent and placed his palms together.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:36.270
Attention! Salute!

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.780
Firing squad!

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:45.950
Take aim!

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:49.030
Fire!

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:13.930
Observe silence!

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:30.030
How ridiculous to die while fighting a fellow Japanese!

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:32.160
At ease!

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:36.750
- This is a battlefield.
- And we've got no allies!

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:39.790
- And now, Mori has fallen.
- Exactly.

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:42.090
If we're attacked, we have to fight back!

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:44.050
That's right. It's either to kill or be killed!

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:45.970
- Mori can't die for nothing!
- There are no rules in war!

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:47.970
We'll never reach Singapore at the rate we're going!

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:49.850
And even so, I'd like you all to pull through.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:55.310
Exclusive defense is not only in times of peace.

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:58.150
It should be our guiding light.

00:13:58.150 --> 00:13:59.650
If we lose sight of it,

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:02.230
our hearts and bodies will be left adrift on this ocean.

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:07.150
What we should be fighting to protect, is present day Japan.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:09.780
The peace that we are so proud of now,

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:12.660
is not something that's maintained solely by guns and weapons.

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:17.160
Whatever the situation, we must always be who we are.

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:21.670
I believe, deep in his heart, that is what Ensign Mori wanted, too.

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:31.800
The lantern at noon? More like a lighthouse on a stormy night.

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:38.020
The US Submarine,

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:40.900
and the Type Two fighter sea planes.

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:44.900
These two battles have made some considerable impact.

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:47.860
I wonder if the influence we have made...

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:51.910
...will only be a slight glitch in the flow of history itself?

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:55.790
Or will it be serious enough to rewrite the outcome of war?

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:57.830
That's something we don't know.

00:14:57.830 --> 00:15:01.960
We must prevent such an incident from repeating itself again.

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:05.210
Regarding the escorts who'll be traveling with Kusaka...

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:08.420
- Executive Officer!
- Yes!

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:12.720
You shall be the one to follow him into Singapore.

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:15.180
Understood.

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:20.020
Carry this with you for self-defense.

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:24.820
Lieutenant Kusaka may be an important guide at sea for us,

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:27.990
but once on land, he'll become the most dangerous person.

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:35.410
Kusaka belongs to this era.

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:37.700
And a man does not change so easily.

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:40.330
Try not to let your guard down against him.

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:42.540
Especially when he mentions his country,

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:45.250
that's when you have to be extra cautious of him.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:48.710
Understood.

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:58.430
Starboard to land, 800!

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:00.140
Both sides, all ahead slow!

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:03.150
- Both sides, all ahead slow!
- 175 degrees, about turn!

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:05.730
- 600 ahead!
- Release stabilizers!

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:07.520
Release stabilizers!

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:09.190
500 ahead!

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:11.360
Port to land, distance 400!

00:16:11.360 --> 00:16:13.030
300 ahead!

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:15.370
- Both sides, to stop!
- 200 ahead!

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:17.280
Both sides, to stop!

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:19.790
Water depth 35 meters, unchanged!

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:23.500
Drop anchor!

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:32.050
A deserted island? It's so quiet.

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:34.590
It's the perfect place to be hiding a ship,

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:37.510
but if there were some girls around, it wouldn't be so boring.

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:41.180
Is it time to talk about girls in an emergency situation like this?

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:44.140
Anchor is in.

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:46.650
Well done. Engine, anchor, all okay.

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:49.020
3000 miles from Ogasawara.

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:51.990
We have done well to make it this far.

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:53.610
We were lucky.

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:57.950
Military notes.

00:16:57.950 --> 00:17:00.660
Right after colonization, mass production of these currency...

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:03.040
...will cause a serious inflation.

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:04.580
Are these ready for use?

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:08.670
Oh, not yet. You gotta soak them in sea water,

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:10.670
rub them, and dry them in the sun.

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:12.670
That was what Lieutenant Kusaka said.

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:14.510
So, where's Kusaka?

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:17.590
Yes. He's been in the library all this while, right?

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:19.600
The library?

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:21.850
I see. Sorry for disrupting.

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:23.390
Executive Officer.

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:26.850
Do you think that we have... made the right choice?

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:31.900
I really don't know.

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:51.840
Something seems to be bothering you.

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:57.300
I'm fine.

00:17:57.300 --> 00:18:00.390
Busy studying even when we're about to go on land?

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:02.180
Books are useful things.

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:04.220
It's able to re-create all the world's knowledge...

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:07.140
...and information inside this head of mine.

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:09.150
What happens after the re-creation?

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:11.400
Knowledge and information is power.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:14.320
For my new life after the time you rescued me...

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:16.280
...it is the most important thing.

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:19.700
Alright then. But there's no need to rush.

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:22.370
You can continue studying after we come back to this ship, right?

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:25.580
Just as I expected, you people really may not be soldiers after all.

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:27.290
What?

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:29.120
Without the experience of war,

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:31.250
and being so used to the long period of peace,

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:34.300
I thought you people wouldn't be likely to understand...

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:36.760
...the current situation and respond to it.

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:39.640
On the battlefield of life and death,

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:42.390
there is no guarantee of one's existence tomorrow.

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:44.890
Neither for me, nor for this ship.

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:59.660
SH-60J, ready for launch! Deploy lifenet!

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:02.910
Deploy beartrap to retaining rail!

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:05.700
The flight to Singapore,

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:09.670
and the negotiations with the officers will take about a week.

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:13.500
To secure the vessel and deliver our food supplies,

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:15.130
that'll take another week.

00:19:15.170 --> 00:19:18.130
Which means this whole operation will run through two whole weeks.

00:19:18.130 --> 00:19:21.800
Yes. With that much time, I should be able to meet your expectations.

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:26.010
This is an unfamiliar land and era for Commander Kadomatsu.

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:29.480
- Please take good care of him.
- Yes. I'll be sure to do so.

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:31.440
Alright. We shall be leaving.

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:33.150
I await your safe return.

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:34.940
Beartrap, open!

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:37.190
Engines to red boost!

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:39.860
Take off!

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:46.160
You shall be a soldier who is under my unit.

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:48.330
We have to do something about your clothes.

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:50.500
Let's get you changed in a nearby town.

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:52.170
I'll need a cap like yours, too.

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:57.960
The stars haven't changed at all in 60 years.

00:19:58.170 --> 00:20:01.510
Captain. I thought I was going to be sent as the escort.

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:05.140
Look, each star is different.

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:06.180
Yes.

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:10.560
You'd eliminate Kusaka once you see him as a danger.

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:14.940
As for Oguri, his character is not firm enough.

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:16.690
However, for Kadomatsu...

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:19.780
He still hasn't reached a judgment of Kusaka.

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:22.200
We need someone like that...

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:24.910
...to draw out the real intentions from Kusaka.

00:20:25.530 --> 00:20:29.330
And I have a feeling that it'll be the key to helping us...

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:32.660
...decide which direction we should be steering this ship in.

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:37.170
Coastline has been sighted! It's the Malay Peninsula.

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:38.550
Topography verified.

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:41.380
I visited this place on a long flight once.

00:20:41.380 --> 00:20:42.800
But this is...

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:47.220
I've heard that they exercise the blackout system, but...

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:49.220
It's unbelievably dark over there!

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:55.350
Did you sleep well last night?

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:57.730
- No.
- Neither did I.

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:01.990
We've no idea what a real war is like.

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:04.150
We learnt from school and history books,

00:21:04.150 --> 00:21:06.620
and act like we understand what war is.

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:09.700
But you have to experience it to really understand.

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:12.620
In this war, some things will change for the Japanese,

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:14.710
and some will not.

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:17.170
It'll be good to watch them closely.

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:24.220
XO, we pray for your success! See you in two weeks on Mirai!

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:27.340
Be careful on your side too! Try not to be discovered!

00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:33.480
I never imagined an autogyro flying at such speeds...

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:36.190
...would be completed in just 60 years from now.

00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:38.020
On the other hand,

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:40.940
your hand pistol hasn't changed that much in shape though.

00:21:40.940 --> 00:21:43.900
I guess it hasn't improved much.

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:49.030
I heard there are wild tigers in Malaya, so I need protection.

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:56.080
Welcome to this era, Commander Kadomatsu.

00:21:56.080 --> 00:21:58.500
Starting from now, you are the guest!

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:17.200
Passing through the distant time

00:22:17.340 --> 00:22:22.410
Just peacefully

00:22:21.910 --> 00:22:34.220
Without losing your way, you walked towards me

00:22:35.350 --> 00:22:47.100
How many times have I grasped tightly those small hands of yours?

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:53.740
Not being able to do anything

00:22:54.310 --> 00:22:59.810
I kept on praying

00:23:01.180 --> 00:23:11.620
Sorrow or agony isn't enough

00:23:13.490 --> 00:23:27.310
That's why now as if I wanted to make up... I'm looking at you

00:23:40.680 --> 00:23:42.640
So this is... a colonized land.

00:23:43.100 --> 00:23:47.930
I'm very sorry, but I'm not the Navy Officer you're looking for.

00:23:47.930 --> 00:23:52.270
The man named Kusaka... what could he be hiding in his heart?

00:23:52.270 --> 00:23:54.650
This place is different from the world you're familiar with.

00:23:54.940 --> 00:23:56.860
And a different history will be unfolding.

00:23:56.860 --> 00:24:00.280
When have the Japanese started to lose their own values?

00:23:59.990 --> 00:24:04.960
Next Episode: Malay Railway

00:24:00.280 --> 00:24:01.950
Come, let us go.

00:24:01.950 --> 00:24:04.620
There's a Japan you don't know of out there.

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:09.960
This story is purely fiction. The names of the
characters and organizations that appear have no
connections with actual people and organizations.
